Getting married at a château is one of those decisions that sets the tone for the whole day. The setting isn’t just a backdrop for photos: it’s the grounds, the stonework and the light that transform the atmosphere of a ceremony. At the Château de la Huberdière, in Touraine, we host weddings for between 30 and 150 guests, on a 14-hectare estate reserved exclusively for you.

Here’s how we envisage organising a wedding at the château, and what this actually means for the bride and groom.

## Why get married in a castle?

A castle for a wedding is not just a beautiful venue. It is a venue that can be hired exclusively, enjoyed over two days, where the celebrations can go on without neighbours or a set timetable.

At La Huberdière, you have the château and its enclosed grounds all to yourselves. No other weddings, no other groups on the same day. A non-religious ceremony under the trees, a reception on the terrace, dinner in the drawing rooms or in a marquee in the grounds: the venue adapts to your plans, not the other way round. Full details of the exclusive hire, capacity and services can be found on the [weddings](/en/mariage) page.

## A wedding at a château 2 hours and 20 minutes from Paris

The Touraine region offers a rare advantage for a wedding: it is beautiful and close by. Nazelles-Négron, where the château is located, is 2 hours and 20 minutes from Paris and just over an hour by train to Tours or Saint-Pierre-des-Corps.

This is an important consideration when hosting guests from the Île-de-France region or further afield. People come to get married in the Loire Valley without making the journey too much of a hassle for their loved ones. Guests arrive on Friday, enjoy Saturday and leave on Sunday, without the strain of a long journey.

## Venues for the ceremony and reception

A wedding takes place in several stages, and each stage deserves its own setting. The estate offers a range of options, which you can combine to suit your schedule and the weather.

- The historic park, the perfect setting for a secular ceremony beneath the centuries-old trees
- The terrace for the reception at sunset
- The large vaulted hall and the dining rooms
- The Orangery or a marquee in the park for the dance floor
- The swimming pool and the paths for the photos the following day

When the weather turns unpredictable, indoor venues take over without disrupting the flow of the day. Nothing is left to chance: we always have a plan for good weather and a fallback plan.

## How many guests? What’s the budget?

The first question from the bride and groom is almost always about capacity. The château can seat up to 150 people for the meal, and the layout can be adapted for more intimate gatherings, starting from around thirty guests.

The cost of a wedding at the château depends on the season, the number of guests and the services provided. As a guide, exclusive use of the estate for a weekend, from Friday to Sunday, including 21 beds, costs between €4,000 and €8,000 depending on the season. There is an additional charge for the provision of tables and chairs for the reception. Rather than a fixed rate, we put together a bespoke proposal once we have understood your plans, with no hidden costs.

One thing couples appreciate is that we don’t charge a corkage fee. You can bring your own wines, champagnes and spirits, and keep control of this often significant expense.

## Accommodating loved ones on site

One of the real luxuries of a castle wedding is being able to accommodate close family on site. The estate’s ten suites, which sleep a total of 21 people, ensure that the bride and groom and their loved ones remain at the heart of the celebrations, without having to travel at night. We gather in the early hours of the morning for a cup of coffee and carry on celebrating without having to worry about the last taxi.

For larger groups, we have a list of partner holiday cottages and hotels within ten minutes’ reach. The same concept of a private estate also caters for [family gatherings](/en/famille) and large dinner parties. The venue is designed to bring people together.

## Service providers, catering and coordination

A successful wedding depends on a good team. We work with trusted local suppliers – caterers, florists and musicians – and we’ll put you in touch with them based on the style you’re looking for. You’re free to bring in your own suppliers if you prefer.

A single point of contact will support you from your first meeting right through to the day after the party. Lodovica brings the warmth of her Italian heritage, whilst I take care of the logistics. This continuity ensures there are no unpleasant surprises and allows you to enjoy your day.

## Getting married at any time of year

People often picture weddings taking place in the summer, but the château is perfect for all seasons. Spring brings a park in full bloom, autumn offers warm colours, and winter provides the cosiness of the drawing rooms and a roaring fire. Each season has its own light and atmosphere, and getting married outside the busiest months also gives you a wider choice of dates.

## Planning your wedding at the château

A beautiful wedding is planned without rushing. We support each couple in choosing a date, organising the two-day event and liaising with suppliers. If you’re extending your stay in the region, our guide to [visiting the châteaux of the Loire Valley](/en/blog/visiter-chateaux-de-la-loire) will help your guests make the most of Touraine.

To check our availability and receive a personalised quote, please visit the [weddings](/en/mariage) page or get in touch. We’ll reply within 24 hours.
